  <title id="bdl06gradientinformed-title">Gradient-informed proposal over the Hamming-one neighborhood of a discrete state</title>
  <desc id="bdl06gradientinformed-desc">A five by five grid of discrete states lies over the contour lines of a smooth function with a large mode at the upper right and a smaller mode at the lower left. The current state x, drawn as a square in the middle, has four neighbors that differ in one coordinate, forming H(x). The gradient of U at x points up and to the right, toward the large mode. Proposal arrows from x to its neighbors are thick toward the right and upper neighbors and thin toward the left and lower ones. The upper neighbor, marked with a star, is the proposed state x prime.</desc>
